==English==

===Etymology 1===
From {{suffix|pot|y|t1=chamberpot|t2=diminutive suffix|lang=en}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|potties}}

# {{lb|en|diminutive}} A [[chamber pot]], ''[[particularly]]'' {{label|en|children}} the [[pot]] [[use]]d when [[toilet-train]]ing [[children]].
#* {{quote-book|title=''In the Money''|author=[[w:William Carlos Williams|William Carlos Williams]]|year=1940|passage=If you just let him know you want him to go on the '''potty''', or anything, he's miles away.}}
#* {{quote-book|title=Your Child Makes Sense: A Guidebook for Parents|author=Edith Buxbaum|year=1949|passage=Mothers very often make the baby and themselves unhappy by setting the child on the '''potty''' every hour.}}
# {{lb|en|diminutive}} [[any|Any]] [[other]] [[device]] or [[place]] for [[urination]] or [[defecation]]: a [[toilet]]; a [[lavatory]]; a [[latrine]]; an [[outhouse]].

